```text
RESOLUTION NO.  ____

ENTITLED: “A RESOLUTION AMENDING THE CITY OF CHEYENNE AND
BOARD OF PUBLIC UTILITIES CONSTRUCTION SPECIFICATIONS
AND STANDARD DRAWINGS, 2014 EDITION.”

WHEREAS, Resolution Numbers 3903, 3970, 4076, 4153, 4321, 4462, 4708, 4942, and
5569 address the Construction Specifications and Standard Drawings for work done within
public rights-of-way in the City of Cheyenne and allow for the City Engineer to revise or amend
the Construction Specifications and Standard Drawings in accordance with good engineering
practices; and

WHEREAS, the City Engineer and the Engineering Department of the Board of Public
Utilities have determined that an amendment to the 2014 Edition of the Construction
Specifications and Standard Drawings is necessary; and

WHEREAS, amendments have been prepared by the Board of Public Utilities; and

WHEREAS, the Board of Public Utilities has provided public notice of its intent to
adopt the amended Construction Specifications and Standard Drawings and provided opportunity
for comment regarding the amended Construction Specifications and Standard Drawings.

NOW, THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, THAT the amended City of Cheyenne and Board of
Public Utilities Construction Specifications and Standard Drawings shall govern construction of
public facilities and construction within public rights-of-way in the City of Cheyenne.

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that the amended City of Cheyenne and Board of
Public Utilities Construction Specifications and Standard Drawings shall be in effect for all
projects and permits approved on or after April 18, 2022.

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that a copy of the amended City of Cheyenne and
Board of Public Utilities Construction Specifications and Standard Drawings shall be kept on file
in the Office of the City Clerk, and made available for public inspection at any time during
business hours.

PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED THIS ____ DAY OF  ______ , 2022.

____________________________________

PATRICK COLLINS, MAYOR

(SEAL)
ATTEST:

___________________________________
KRISTINA F. JONES, CITY CLERK
By Stefanie Boster at 9:53 am, Apr 04, 2022
```

### Page 2 of 522

```text
Board of Public
Utilities
Cheyenne Water and Sewer Departments
2416 Snyder Ave.
Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001
(307) 637-6460
www.cheyennebopu.org

Memo

To:
Mayor Patrick Collins
City Council
From:
Bryce Dorr, P.E., Capital Projects Supervisor
Date:
March 25, 2022
Subject:
2022 Amendment to the City of Cheyenne & Board of Public Utilities Construction Specifications and
Standard Drawings

Design engineers and contractors rely on the City of Cheyenne & Board of Public
Utilities Specifications and Standard Drawings (Specs) to provide design and
construction standards specific to our community.  The Specs are used for City and
BOPU funded projects, as well as development projects within Cheyenne and the
BOPU service area.

The Specs were last updated in 2014.  Since the last update, staff has compiled
comments and monitored trends in the water/wastewater construction industry;
some of which were relatively significant.  In Fall 2019, BOPU and City staff agreed
that BOPU could update its sections with the Specs independent of the other
sections.

Beginning in 2020, BOPU held regular meetings to perform a complete review of
the Specs.  The BOPU review committee included staff from the Inspection, Capital
Projects, Distribution, Collection, and Support Services departments.  The review
process took nearly two years to complete.  On November 29, 2021, BOPU
released the updated Specs for 45-day public review period.  BOPU received public
comment and amended the Specs accordingly.  In general, Staff updated Specs to
clarify language, update allowable manufacturers, and update references to allow
most recent version.  A summary of BOPU-specific section technical updates in the
Specs is listed below:

 SECTION 02051 - ABANDON PIPE SYSTEMS
Manhole abandonment language removed and replaced with
reference to section 02050 Removal and Disposal of Structures and
Obstructions.
 SECTION 02645 - FIRE HYDRANTS
Storz connections added on 5-inch intake per request of Fire
Department and required materials be new and less than 2 years old.
```

### Page 3 of 522

```text
Board of Public
Utilities
Cheyenne Water and Sewer Departments
2416 Snyder Ave.
Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001
(307) 637-6460
www.cheyennebopu.org

 SECTION 02665 - WATER DISTRIBUTION AND TRANSMISSION
SYSTEMS
Ductile iron listed as a non-preferred pipe material.  PVC pipe
thickness updated based on pipe diameter.  Casing pipe and spacer
material updated to allow PVC and plastic to reduce costs and limit
corrosion.  Changed preferred water service line material from copper
to HDPE.  Changed meter pit style to ease installation and
maintenance.  Updated water/sewer crossings to simplify and reflect
10-States Standards.  Allow combination fire/domestic services (≤ 2”)
to promote residential fire sprinkler systems.  Reduced meter vault
sizing and allowed use of manhole to reduce cost.
 SECTION 02667 - COLD WATER METERS (⅝" through 12") [REMOVED]
 SECTION 02670 - HYDROSTATIC TESTING
Removed detailed instruction and referenced AWWA standard.
 SECTION 02675 - DISINFECTION
Removed detailed instruction and referenced AWWA standard.
 SECTION 02700 - SANITARY SEWER SYSTEMS
Manhole troughs to be constructed with pipe and fittings to reduce
maintenance and improve design life.  Outside drop manholes to be
constructed with 45° bend to improve flow.  Inserta Tee service
connections disallowed due to complications with maintenance of
sewer main; saddle type connections upgraded to styles that reduce
likelihood of root intrusion and sewer backups.  Force main material
updated to be PVC.  Updated manhole pipe penetration seals and
added waterproofing of all manholes to reduce inflow/infiltration of
storm/ground water to maximize capacity of sewer mains for future
growth.  Updated adjustment ring allowance to balance construction
flexibility and structural reliability.  Manholes repaired due to failed
leakage test shall be repaired from outside to improve longevity of
repair.  Reordered EXECUTION section to match chronological order

BOPU staff also updated the Standard Drawings to reflect the updated
specifications.  Staff attempted to simplify and clarify drawings to improve ease of
use.

Presuming this amendment is approved, the BOPU and City Engineer’s Office is
proposing that the effective date will be on or after Monday, April 18, 2022.  All
projects approved on or after that date will be required to conform to this
amendment whereas all projects approved prior to that date will continue to be
constructed under current specifications unless otherwise approved by the BOPU
and City Engineer’s Office.
```

