stakes and marks. If construction stakes and marks are destroyed
and/or disturbed by the CONTRACTOR, then the CONTRACTOR
shall have them replaced at his cost or the price for replacement
shall be deducted from the payment of the work.

1.06
DUTIES OF THE INSPECTOR

A.
As employed by the Contracting Agency, Inspectors shall be
authorized to inspect all work and materials furnished. Inspections
may extend to all or part of the work and to the preparation,
fabrication or manufacturing of materials being used.

B.
The Inspector shall not be authorized to issue instructions contrary
to the plans and specifications or to act as foreman for the
CONTRACTOR.

C.
The Inspector shall have the authority to reject work or materials
until any questions at issue can be referred to and decided upon by
the ENGINEER.
